From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristjan Sillmann <kristjan.h.s@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sdk-audio-prepare-race

Stream ids end to end (plan 2026-11-10 answer-conn-and-prepare-race P2.a1): stream A sent Complete and closed,
the gateway freed its slot while vic-anim still played A's buffered audio; stream B was admitted, its Prepare was
refused (PrepareFailed), it closed without Complete, and the gateway's close-Cancel (sdk-audio-orphan) cut A.
Nothing carried a stream id, so no hop could tell B's messages from A's.
vic-cloud gateway: numbers each ExternalAudioStreamPlayback and stamps the id into every Prepare/Chunk/Complete/
Cancel it forwards (a client value is overwritten), including its own close-Cancel. A status whose stream_id is
not this stream's is neither forwarded nor its verdict (logs my-vector.SdkAudioOrphan); completeSent is gone,
the id match replaces it.
gateway proto: stream_id on ExternalAudioStreamPrepare/Chunk/Complete/Cancel and ExternalAudioStreamResponse
(new field numbers, proto3 backward compatible).
CLAD: stream_id on ExternalAudioPrepare/Chunk/Complete/Cancel, streamId on AudioStreamStatusEvent; first in Chunk
and StatusEvent because the CPPLite emitter needs a uint_32 4-aligned. ExternalAudioChunk is 1030 bytes, under
the emitter's --max-message-size 1400 (EngineToRobot stays 1219).
vic-engine: SDKComponent copies the id from the gateway requests into the CLAD messages and from
AudioStreamStatusEvent into ExternalAudioStreamResponse; its own chunk-size failures carry the chunk's id.
vic-anim: Prepare remembers the accepted id; Chunk/Complete/Cancel with another id are dropped (my-vector.
SdkAudioOrphan names both ids; a foreign stream's chunks log once); every status is stamped, a refused or failed
Prepare with the refused stream's id, so the gateway takes it as that stream's verdict and sends no close-Cancel.
Falsifier: voiceprobe race, C's PlaybackComplete lands at or after A's audio end (FAIL before: 1.013 s early).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
